Portuguese Football Federation announced on Saturday that it has provisionally suspended star attacker Cristiano Ronaldo and opened disciplinary proceedings against the 41-year-old over his decision to walk out on the national team last month. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a852fd72-c4af-11f1-9559-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272841554245.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a852fd72-c4af-11f1-9559-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272841554245.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e5c29aa-c4b0-11f1-818e-e562f9b17c93</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:02:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a852fd72-c4af-11f1-9559-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26272841554245.jpg">© Armando Franca, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen says advancing against Houthis around key Bab al-Mandab strait</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-yemen-says-forces-made-advances-against-houthis-around-key-waterway</link><description>
Yemen said Saturday that forces were advancing against the Houthis around the Bab al-Mandab strait. This comes a week after the country's Saudi-backed government announced that it was initiating a counter-offensive to take back territory seized by the pro-Iran group during last month's lightning offensive. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63b80868-c4ac-11f1-b128-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279449082196.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63b80868-c4ac-11f1-b128-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279449082196.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d761d14c-c4aa-11f1-acd0-877b784b702e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:45:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63b80868-c4ac-11f1-b128-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279449082196.jpg">© Southern Giants Brigades Media Office via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Palestinian president Abbas postpones legislative elections, sets presidential poll for September 2027</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-palestinian-president-abbas-postpones-legislative-elections-to-september-2027</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">e57a9128-c4a1-11f1-b006-c9c9837a94ba</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:58:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Palestinian president Abbas postpones legislative, presidential elections to September 2027</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-palestinian-president-abbas-postpones-legislative-elections-to-september-2027</link><description>
⁠⁠Palestinian president ​Mahmoud ​Abbas announced on Saturday that legislative ⁠elections would be postponed from November ​28 to September ​11, 2027, the ​official Palestinian news agency ⁠WAFA reported. In his presidential decree, Abbas set the next presidential elections for that day as well.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f8bf20-b818-11f1-a7c2-4d88a6d99c48/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25356421415725.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f8bf20-b818-11f1-a7c2-4d88a6d99c48/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25356421415725.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5813cf5c-c4a1-11f1-9901-7958fca43b77</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:56:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f8bf20-b818-11f1-a7c2-4d88a6d99c48/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25356421415725.jpg">© Nasser Nasser; AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>October 7 scars push Israel's first-time voters to right</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-october-7-scars-push-israel-s-first-time-voters-to-right</link><description>
Like hundreds of thousands of Israelis, Amihai will be of voting age for the first time since Hamas carried out its attack on October 7, 2023. When he casts his ballot this month, he has one priority above all -- security.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ee7f0b72-c498-11f1-b452-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-120855-121055-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ee7f0b72-c498-11f1-b452-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-120855-121055-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f306d724-c498-11f1-b126-9f710ebc361a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:01:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hunger and malnutrition stalk Gazans, a year on from ceasefire</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-hunger-and-malnutrition-stalk-gazans-a-year-on-from-ceasefire</link><description>
Every day, Gazan mother Niyaha al-Masri spends six exhausting hours or more queueing at a community kitchen in the hope of getting some food for her family. It has been a year since a ceasefire between Hamas and Israel was supposed to allow food to flood into the ruined territory, yet widespread hunger persists there.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fdcc1e0-c498-11f1-bd91-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-120622-120834-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8fdcc1e0-c498-11f1-bd91-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-120622-120834-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">946cafc2-c498-11f1-b7bf-0d6231622a12</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:00:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Severe injuries at French student protests draw scrutiny to police tactics</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261010-injuries-french-student-protests-draw-scrutiny-to-police-tactics</link><description>
Twenty-four investigations have been opened by French police watchdog IGPN into incidents linked to the ongoing high school protest movement, the interior ministry said. The police response has reignited calls to scrap rubber bullets and launcher-fired riot-control weapons, long denounced by rights groups and UN experts as dangerous and excessive. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc604004-c491-11f1-b892-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-10T050008Z-2085041987-RC24ZNA99AZV-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST-POLICE-VIOLENCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc604004-c491-11f1-b892-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-10T050008Z-2085041987-RC24ZNA99AZV-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST-POLICE-VIOLENCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d008b3a2-c491-11f1-84a4-3396ede61a40</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:20:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc604004-c491-11f1-b892-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-10T050008Z-2085041987-RC24ZNA99AZV-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST-POLICE-VIOLENCE.jpg">© Pedro Nunes, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Navanethem 'Navi' Pillay wins the Nobel Peace Prize</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-navanethem-navi-pillay-wins-the-nobel-peace-prize</link><description>
Former UN human rights chief Navanethem "Navi" Pillay, a judge at the International Court of Justice, won the Nobel Peace Prize on Friday in Oslo, Norway.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4d53528-c3fd-11f1-8f45-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26282459763051.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4d53528-c3fd-11f1-8f45-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26282459763051.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58d1def6-c489-11f1-8ae4-df7b0c47944f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:25:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>India's 'cockroach' movement: "This is unprecedented"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-india-s-cockroach-movement-this-is-unprecedented</link><description>
Indian police detained Abhijeet Dipke, head of the satirical Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) movement, on Saturday ahead of a major protest against the Election Commission, the party said.

"This is unprecedented," our guest Subir Sinha, director of the SOAS South Asia Institute, says.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2fe79dce-c488-11f1-b92e-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-090404-091253-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2fe79dce-c488-11f1-b92e-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-090404-091253-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34910a40-c488-11f1-9d54-1dbe1941f599</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:20:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>India detains 'cockroach' leaders ahead of election protest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-india-detains-cockroach-leaders-ahead-of-election-protest</link><description>
Indian police detained the head of the satirical "cockroach" online movement on Saturday, the group said, ahead of a major protest against the Election Commission that triggered strict security measures. Our correspondent Navodita Kumari tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b855ea2-c483-11f1-a9b2-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-100108-100645-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b855ea2-c483-11f1-a9b2-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-100108-100645-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">208b5a5a-c483-11f1-a48c-6d26eb27a2bd</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:18:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Scientists conduct microgravity experiments on parabolic flights</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-france-scientists-conduct-microgravity-experiments-on-parabolic-flights</link><description>
This week in Bordeaux, the CNES, the French space agency, launched a microgravity research campaign with scientists from all over the world. It gave them the opportunity to conduct experiments in weightlessness during parabolic flights aboard a specially equipped Airbus, without having to send their equipment into space.
 
Our reporters James André and Sylvain Rousseau joined them on board.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd6111ca-c485-11f1-ac8c-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-101139-101405-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd6111ca-c485-11f1-ac8c-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-101139-101405-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">021371a4-c486-11f1-bbab-27c3858813e0</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:15:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump hails Russia deal to release diesel as midterms loom</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261010-trump-hails-russia-deal-to-release-diesel-as-midterms-loom</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Friday that he had secured Russia's agreement for a major release of diesel, as he eased war sanctions on Moscow in a push to lower energy costs ahead of midterm elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7955640e-c484-11f1-b5a3-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-100736-100929-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7955640e-c484-11f1-b5a3-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261010-100736-100929-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e98c42e-c484-11f1-a959-b9a48b81784d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:12:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Russian strikes on Ukraine kill at least 15 in Zaporizhzhia, cause power outages in Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-live-russian-strikes-on-ukraine-zaporizhzhia-kill-least-seven-including-children</link><description>
Russian strikes on the southeastern Ukrainian city of Zaporizhzhia killed at least 15 people, including three children, regional authorities said on Saturday. The attack also caused "large-scale power outages" in the capital Kyiv and the surrounding region. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e19554c-c4a8-11f1-afba-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T064056Z-387380484-RC2GZNAV9HM8-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-ZAPORIZHZHIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e19554c-c4a8-11f1-afba-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T064056Z-387380484-RC2GZNAV9HM8-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-ZAPORIZHZHIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6cbaa19a-c485-11f1-9885-e513ae9fb83b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:41:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9e19554c-c4a8-11f1-afba-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T064056Z-387380484-RC2GZNAV9HM8-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-ZAPORIZHZHIA.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'All human emotions': French astronaut Sophie Adenot returns to Earth</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-all-human-emotion-french-astronaut-sophie-adenot-first-words-since-returning-earth</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot said she experienced “the full range of human emotions, from the most joyful to the most difficult” during her eight months in space, speaking on Saturday in Cologne, Germany, in her first public appearance since returning to Earth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4dc35d4a-c471-11f1-89b7-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-10T055758Z-1398580967-RC250OAPT20V-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ESA-ASTRONAUT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4dc35d4a-c471-11f1-89b7-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-10T055758Z-1398580967-RC250OAPT20V-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ESA-ASTRONAUT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b183a050-c481-11f1-8de0-8f0559b72f8a</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:09:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4dc35d4a-c471-11f1-89b7-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-10T055758Z-1398580967-RC250OAPT20V-RTRMADP-3-GERMANY-ESA-ASTRONAUT.jpg">© Thilo Schmuelgen, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US, Europe and Ukraine hold 'constructive discussions' on joint plan to end war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261010-us-ukrainians-europeans-discuss-new-ideas-to-end-war-diesel</link><description>
US, Ukrainian and European negotiators held talks in Miami on Friday to seek a common proposal to end the war in Ukraine, as President Donald Trump's decision to ease restrictions on Russian fuel drew criticism from lawmakers and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69175476-c47f-11f1-a476-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T050009Z-1359303607-RC2SDNA1852R-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-EUROPE-GAS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69175476-c47f-11f1-a476-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T050009Z-1359303607-RC2SDNA1852R-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-EUROPE-GAS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e9ab8ea-c47e-11f1-b3d1-650afb66e3ea</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:47:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/69175476-c47f-11f1-a476-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T050009Z-1359303607-RC2SDNA1852R-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-EUROPE-GAS.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>‘So safe you could drink it’: Scientists and pesticide victims fear an EU rollback</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261010-so-safe-you-could-drink-it-scientists-and-pesticide-victims-fear-an-eu-rollback</link><description>
For decades, French farmers sprayed pesticides they were told were harmless. Many have since fallen ill, grappling with cancers and other diseases caused by exposure. As the EU prepares to vote on a package that would end regular safety reviews of most pesticides, victims, doctors and scientists warn it could keep harmful products on the market for longer.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdd5d364-c3e0-11f1-8680-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25132558305552.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdd5d364-c3e0-11f1-8680-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25132558305552.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2418163a-c3df-11f1-882c-f7781fb761f1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:10:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdd5d364-c3e0-11f1-8680-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25132558305552.jpg">© Charlie Neibergall, AP</source><dc:creator>Lara BULLENS</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>India's 'cockroach' movement chief detained ahead of major protest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261010-india-s-cockroach-movement-chief-detained-ahead-of-major-protest</link><description>
Police detained hundreds of protesters, including movement leaders, in the Indian capital on Saturday as authorities deployed thousands of security personnel, suspended transport and telecommunications services, and imposed sweeping restrictions to thwart a youth-led demonstration demanding the resignation of the country's election chief.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/166aa39a-c475-11f1-9483-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/a98f7fd30fe0d596e56bff31cb889f1597cde274.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/166aa39a-c475-11f1-9483-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/a98f7fd30fe0d596e56bff31cb889f1597cde274.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1725410a-c475-11f1-b7f4-2fe66f5d119b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 06:37:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/166aa39a-c475-11f1-9483-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/a98f7fd30fe0d596e56bff31cb889f1597cde274.jpg">© Manan Vatsyayana, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Palestinians struggle to find food in Gaza one year after ceasefire</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-hunger-and-malnutrition-stalk-gazans-a-year-on-from-ceasefire</link><description>
Widespread hunger remains persistent in the Gaza Strip despite the ceasefire agreement between Hamas and Israel a year ago that was supposed to allow more food into the Palestinian territory. A new study published on Thursday by Médecins du Monde reported that 93 percent of pregnant or breastfeeding women had symptoms of anaemia, which is closely linked to malnutrition.  
